timeshift-on-demand (0.1.0~dev6) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Fixed the GTK monitor window showing nothing during a real backup
    then jumping straight to a completion notification. Two independent
    buffering layers: timeshift's own stdout is fully block-buffered
    (not line-buffered) when not attached to a terminal, and the backup
    helper's own `output=$(...)` capture independently buffered
    everything internally regardless. Fixed with `stdbuf -o0 -e0` on
    the timeshift call plus a `tee`-based capture (also unbuffered)
    instead of command substitution, so output reaches the log file --
    and the monitor window watching it -- as it's produced. Verified
    live: a real GTK screenshot mid-run shows genuine partial progress,
    not a blank window.
  * Documented that on-demand backups are not automatically pruned by
    Timeshift's own retention settings (confirmed via real log
    evidence, correcting an earlier wrong claim) -- added to the
    Dashboard's advisory label and README.md's Known Limitations.

