timeshift-on-demand (0.1.0~dev4) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Fixed 2 real bugs in the resume-from-suspend hook, found via actual
    suspend/resume testing on the Samsung RF511:
    - The hook launched the prompt via `runuser -u <user>`, which
      creates a brand-new PAM login session -- systemd-logind killed it
      almost immediately, before the prompt script could even start.
      Switched to `systemd-run --uid=... --collect --`, a plain
      transient service rather than a login session, so logind has
      nothing to tear down.
    - The hook was launching the prompt once per "active" loginctl
      session, including SSH connections (Type=tty) alongside the real
      desktop session (Type=wayland/x11) -- a tty session can never show
      a GUI dialog, so this was pure waste and a real risk of two
      parallel backup attempts. Now filtered to wayland/x11 sessions
      only.
  * Both fixes verified end-to-end: a manual re-test with the backup
    drive connected reached the zenity confirmation dialog, which was
    visually confirmed on-screen.

