timeshift-on-demand (0.1.0~dev2) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * src/ reworked: all privileged calls go through pkexec against the
    bundled helpers (backup, cron-fix, and a new read-only snapshot-list
    helper — timeshift --list needs root unconditionally on every
    install, confirmed by testing every flag timeshift --help describes
    as a query). New config.py for per-user XDG settings; new Settings
    tab for drive selection (no more hardcoded UUID); dead systemd-unit
    status reporting dropped from status.py.
  * Added the login-autostart and resume-from-suspend auto-prompt path
    (timeshift-on-demand-prompt + timeshift-on-demand-monitor, zenity
    confirm + live monitor window), independent of the GTK app.
  * Fixed a real, launch-blocking bug found via an actual screenshot
    during testing: app.py never called show_all(), so every tab's
    content was silently invisible despite the window itself mapping
    correctly with no errors.
  * Dashboard's snapshot glance now carries a permanent advisory that
    it is read-only and "Open Timeshift" is the only way to actually
    work with snapshot data; the privileged list call is restricted to
    explicit user actions (open, manual Refresh, post-backup) and
    deliberately excluded from the 30s auto-refresh timer, to avoid
    repeated authentication prompts just for having the window open.
  * Functionally tested end-to-end (mocked pkexec/zenity/notify-send,
    sandboxed XDG dirs) and live in the running GUI app
    (screenshot + xdotool-driven clicks) — see PROJECT.md for the full
    verification log. Not yet attempted: dpkg-buildpackage/lintian, and
    a real suspend/resume test of the resume-hook.

